===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|table cloth|table-cloth}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|tabyllcloth}}, {{m|enm|table cloth}}, {{m|enm|tabylle clothe}}, a partial translation of earlier {{der|en|enm|bord cloth}}, {{m|enm|bordcloth|t=tablecloth}}, from {{der|en|ang|bordclāþ}}, equivalent to {{compound|en|table|cloth}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-tablecloth.wav|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[cloth]] used to [[cover]] and [[protect]] a [[table]], especially for a [[dining table]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1893|author=w:Horatio Alger, Jr.|title=Facing the World
|passage=Just across the field stood a small house. In the yard the week's washing was hung out. Among the articles was a red '''tablecloth'''.}}

